      "detail": "A theta' = A theta holds to a max relative residual of 1.3e-12 in float64, so the forgery is exact in exact arithmetic. It is not bit-identical once the network runs the conv in float32: max |dlogit| over the test set is 4.00e-03-6.82e-02 across the variants, against a 4.89e-03 float32 reduction-order noise floor measured by re-running the same passport at a different batch size, on logits of magnitude up to 21.8. Functionally: 4 of 5 forged passports reproduce the original test accuracy to all 4 decimals, changing at worst 0.34% of predictions, while a random passport costs 25.0 pp."
    },
    "N1_forgery_survives_a_distribution_check_on_theta_p": {
